      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-15T11:11:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry, but that is not the proper way to do this, if a user can access your ioctl that way, they can easily change their sid as well.  Please fix your out-of-tree monitorhang kernel driver properly to prevent this from happening at all, as that sounds like the real issue to fix here, not paper over it by attempting to access a SID.",
      "parentUuid": "6a09de8c_c36a715c",
      "revId": "9c84b168942e270be4126df6f8b3c85c6249048b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
